-- 0105_world_kitchen_recipes: recipes aimed at non-Indian search markets.
--
-- WHY. The catalogue's 48 published recipes are all Indian preparations, so
-- the site is invisible to anyone searching for the dishes these same
-- staples belong in -- emmer pasta, tahini, sesame halva, cracked-wheat
-- tabbouleh, field-pea fritters. These 100 recipes span roughly forty
-- cuisines and target that demand in English, which is the only foreign
-- search traffic reachable today: every language currently shares one URL,
-- so until per-locale URLs and an hreflang cluster exist, a translated
-- recipe cannot rank in a non-English market however good it is.
--
-- Each recipe names its own `cuisine` (migration 0104) rather than
-- inheriting a site-wide default, so the structured data stops claiming
-- every recipe is Indian. Each is written individually against a
-- generator script that rejects duplicate slugs, duplicate titles, a
-- shared closing sentence, or fewer than 8 steps/ingredients -- the same
-- bar migration 0102 applied to hand-written discussions, and the
-- opposite of how the `rcp_truegrit_` set was built (identical boilerplate
-- around a swapped ingredient name).
--
-- Every product reference is a real, live product slug from migration 0095;
-- there are no product placeholders here.
PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;

